WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.437
Flexbox: one line, two axes, and the declaration that lines up a header.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.006
A news site header. A title on the left, links on the right.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.271
Out of the box, it's a stack. Block elements pile up, one under another.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.943
One declaration fixes that: display: flex, on the header.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:28.683
The header is now a flex container. Its direct children, the h1 and the nav, become flex items, side by side.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.172
Flexbox is one-dimensional. It lays items along a line: the main axis.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.980
By default that runs left to right. Across it runs the cross axis, top to bottom.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:46.137
Every alignment property is named after an axis, never after left or right.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.116
justify-content works along the main axis. flex-start packs the items at the start.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:58.329
center puts half the leftover space before the first item, and half after the last.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:04.819
space-between sends the first item to one edge and the last to the other. Title left, nav right.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.536
align-items works across the line. flex-start hugs the top.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.312
center puts both items in the middle of the header's height.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.669
That's the whole header: three declarations, two axes.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.637
Now the links. The nav holds a ul, and the ul holds the li elements.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:30.823
Put display: flex on the nav, and nothing changes. The links stay stacked.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:37.727
Flex only reaches direct children. The nav's only child is the ul, so the ul is the single item.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.252
Make the ul the container, with a gap of 1rem. Now the links sit in a row.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.644
Change flex-direction to column, and the axes turn.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.927
The main axis now runs top to bottom. The cross axis runs left to right.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:02:00.523
justify-content didn't change. It still follows the main axis, so it now moves items vertically.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:07.714
align-items moves them horizontally. And vertical centring only shows if the container is taller than its content.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:14.089
Last question: how wide is each item? Flexbox works in two steps.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.168
First, every item gets its basis: its width, or its content size.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.595
Then it compares the total with the container, and shares out the difference.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.783
By default, items never grow. The leftover space just stays empty.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:36.021
Give two items flex: 1 and flex: 2, in a 600px container. Both start from 0.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:40.968
flex: 1 is shorthand for flex-grow: 1, flex-shrink: 1, flex-basis: 0%.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:46.962
600px to share, in the ratio 1 to 2. 200px, and 400px.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.881
Too wide instead? flex-shrink takes the excess back, the same way.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.622
Practise it with the Flexbox playground in CSS.
